    <h2>Key Factors That Influence CPM Rates</h2>
    <p>
      CPM rates in programmatic ad auctions are dynamically set by five fundamental variables:
    </p>

    <div class="step-guide">
      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>1. Geographic Location (Audience Purchasing Power)</h3>
        <p>
          Ad inventory is priced by geographic tiers:
          <br />
          • <strong>Tier 1 (Premium CPM: $15 – $40+):</strong> United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, Germany.
          <br />
          • <strong>Tier 2 (Moderate CPM: $5 – $14):</strong> Spain, Brazil, Poland, South Africa, Mexico.
          <br />
          • <strong>Tier 3 (Budget CPM: $0.50 – $4):</strong> India, Indonesia, Philippines, Egypt.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>2. Industry Niche & Commercial Intent</h3>
        <p>
          Advertisers bid aggressively for audiences searching for high-margin financial products or enterprise software. A financial advisor is willing to pay a $50 CPM because a single client can generate thousands of dollars in revenue.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>3. Seasonality (The Q4 Budget Surge)</h3>
        <p>
          CPM rates follow annual corporate budget cycles. During <strong>Q4 (October to December)</strong>, holiday e-commerce budgets drive CPMs up by 50% to 100%. Conversely, in <strong>Q1 (January to February)</strong>, advertiser budgets reset, causing CPMs to drop sharply.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>4. Ad Viewability & Placement Format</h3>
        <p>
          Non-skippable video pre-rolls and above-the-fold display banners command higher CPMs than skippable ads or below-the-fold banners that users never scroll down to see.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="step-item">
        <h3>5. Click-Through Rate (CTR) & Ad Relevance</h3>
        <p>
          Ad networks reward high-converting, relevant creatives. An ad with a 2.5% CTR receives a higher relevance quality score, which lowers the auction bid required to win ad impressions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>How This CPM Calculator Works</h2>
